puller: EDEN_NX2_ACQUIRE_REFENCE=1 releases fences again while an acquire waits

Port of Djihads80/Eglantine 90ff431884 (kraibse, branch fix/oot-blackscreen, 2026-11-05).
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the core.

The source commit: with Balanced fences Ocarina froze after a while, channel 2 waiting on a semaphore
0x13 releases behind and no channel moving. A semaphore release is a payload query, which delayed
fence operations keep in the query cache until the next fence. An acquire released the fences once
and then suspended; the recheck only read the semaphore. The recheck now releases the fences again,
at most once a millisecond, while operations are delayed.

Set this with EDEN_GPU_FENCE=balanced or accurate. Those modes are the ones the freeze needs, and
this core has the partner fix 1b594aa6b6 already, as SubmitDeferredWork.

Changed from the source: behind the switch, since accuracy High also counts as delayed here, so
Bananza with Fast GPU off would change too. It goes through ReleaseFencesOnBack (0041), which runs
the release on the split's back and waits. Unset, one static bool more per recheck. Default fences at
Low accuracy never enter it.

Runs on the PS5: same core path. Pool memory: none.

Co-authored-by: kraibse <33869366+kraibse@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/src/video_core/engines/puller.cpp b/src/video_core/engines/puller.cpp
index 9e4b8ae3b7..5b34be8bab 100644
--- a/src/video_core/engines/puller.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/engines/puller.cpp
@@ -107,6 +107,26 @@ bool Puller::CanResumeAcquire(DmaPusher& dma_pusher) {
     if (pending_acquire->Matches(current)) {
         return true;
     }
+    // EDEN_NX2_ACQUIRE_REFENCE=1: with delayed fence operations (Balanced or Accurate fences,
+    // accurate GPU), a release queued after the acquire released the fences waits in the caches for
+    // the next fence. With every channel waiting none comes: release them again now and then.
+    static const bool refence = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_ACQUIRE_REFENCE");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    const bool delayed = refence && (Settings::IsGPUFenceBehaviorDefault()
+                                         ? Settings::IsGPULevelHigh()
+                                         : Settings::IsGPUFenceBehaviorBalanced() ||
+                                               Settings::IsGPUFenceBehaviorAccurate());
+    if (delayed && std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - pending_acquire->last_fences >=
+                       std::chrono::milliseconds{1}) {
+        pending_acquire->last_fences = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+        ReleaseFencesOnBack(dma_pusher.rasterizer);
+        if (Nx2SemaphoreWaiters::Get().Latched(this) ||
+            pending_acquire->Matches(ReadSemaphoreWord(dma_pusher, pending_acquire->address))) {
+            return true;
+        }
+    }
     if (!pending_acquire->reported &&
         std::chrono::steady_clock::now() - pending_acquire->since > std::chrono::seconds{2}) {
         pending_acquire->reported = true;
@@ -255,6 +275,7 @@ void Puller::ProcessSemaphoreTriggerMethod(DmaPusher& dma_pusher) {
             .value = regs.semaphore_sequence,
             .operation = static_cast<u32>(op),
             .since = std::chrono::steady_clock::now(),
+            .last_fences = std::chrono::steady_clock::now(),
             .reported = false,
         };
         if (op != GpuSemaphoreOperation::AcquireEqual && op != GpuSemaphoreOperation::AcquireGequal &&
